steps.explanation:
$v_C(t_1) = V_s\left(1 - e^{-t_1/\tau}\right)$ = {{Vx|V}} means $e^{-t_1/\tau} = 1 - {{p}}$ = {{1 - p}}, so
$\tau = \frac{-t_1}{\ln(1 - v/V_s)}$ = {{t1|s}} / {{-ln(1 - p)||3}} = {{Rx*C|s}}
$R = \tau/C$ = {{Rx*C|s}} / {{C|F}} = **{{Rx|Ω}}**. A smaller $R$ would charge faster and overshoot the point; a larger one would pass below it.
